out.push(S('Stage 5 · Read'));
out.push(A('**1** Eleven drivers have asked him about it, **two minutes each**, and he has been able to tell each of them nothing — and **two of them have told their families that the service is going**. The cost is counted in other people\'s time and in two families.'));
out.push(A('**2** The roads office, the directorate, his own manager, and the depot clerk. **Each one would have been a sentence he could check in one telephone call**, and the sentence as printed cannot be checked by anybody at all.'));
out.push(A('**3** Because a driver can **act** on it: he can ask Mr Mroueh, he knows the date, and he can tell his family a date instead of a rumour. _A signed notice is a thing you can act on. The one on the wall is a thing you can only worry about._'));
out.push(A('The paragraph to teach is **who is in the sentence**, because of what it does rhetorically: listing the four people he tried **shows the work**, and without it the claim that nobody will go in is only his opinion. The other move worth naming is _what I am not saying_ — _for all I know the second bus is going_ — which keeps the note about the notice. Without that sentence the manager answers a note about the bus, and the notice stays on the wall.'));
